  "question": {
    "text": "A series LCR circuit is connected to an alternating source of emf E. The current amplitude at resonant frequency is $I_0$. If the value of resistance R becomes twice of its initial value then amplitude of current at resonance will be"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "$2 \\mathrm{I}_0$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$I_0$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$\\frac{\\mathrm{I}_0}{2}$",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "$\\frac{\\mathrm{I}_0}{\\sqrt{2}}$",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "C"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "Initially, $\\mathrm{I}_0=\\frac{\\varepsilon_{\\mathrm{m}}}{\\mathrm{R}}$\nFinally, $\\mathrm{I}_0^1=\\frac{\\varepsilon_{\\mathrm{m}}}{2 \\mathrm{R}}=\\frac{\\mathrm{I}_0}{2}$"
  }
}